  <!--
    The message catalogue, neutral English (Part 8).

    One entry per event identifier, keyed E<number>_<Name>: the NUMBER is the contract, the name
    is for reading. Keying by name alone would collide - DataRootChosen is 4001 in the control and
    4002 in the display, and the two say different things.

    Placeholders are NAMED and must match the [LoggerMessage] declaration exactly; a test in
    DnDOverlay.Core.Tests compares the two and fails on any entry that is missing, spare or
    differently spelled. German arrives in M5b as LogMessages.de.resx, against these same keys.
  -->
